 Open Government Licence providing it is done so, acknowledging both the source and NRW\u0027s copyright. It is the recipient\u0027s responsibility to ensure the data is fit for the intended purpose.\tContains Natural Resources Wales information © Natural Resources Wales and Database Right. All rights Reserved.\tOpen Government Licence\t\t\tValid\t-\nNRW_DS125330\tVisitor safety zones\totherRestrictions\tno limitations\tThis dataset is wholly owned by NRW Data should not be made available publicly. Printed maps may need to be made public, but this should be done at the site manager’s discretion along with approval by the Specialist Advisor Recreation Safety.\totherRestrictions\t© CNC/NRW  NRW does NOT grant permission to third parties to re-use or disseminate this dataset.  Contains Natural Resources Wales information © Natural Resources Wales and database right. Note buffering around linear and point features mean that area calculations cannot be achieved accurately. These should not be undertaken. Printing of maps should be conducted on the appropriate visitor safety zonation template and printed maps are only accurate as to the date they were printed. Site managers must contact the data custodian to ensure this data aligns with their public safety risk assessments. To edit or print a map of the zones, email the Data and Content Advisor (Recreation) to ensure the correct template and formatting are used. Data does not include ExEAW land as yet.  PRoW is a NRW representation only. The NRW estate is z ned according to VSG risk categories as illustrated on the map. Although these zones appear with hard boundaries, they are indicative only and care must be exercised if zooming in closely and zones are not sharply defined regarding the application of control measures.\t\t\t\t\tUnknown\t-\nNRW_DS125200\tWater Framework Directive (WFD) Transitional Waterbodies Cycle 3\totherRestrictions\tno limitations\tThere are no access restrictions on this data. NRW may release, publish or disseminate it freely.\totherRestrictions\t© CNC/NRW All rights Reserved. Contains Ordnance Survey Data. Ordnance Survey Licence number AC0000849444. Crown Copyright and Database Right Data may be re-used under the terms of the Open Government Licence providing it is done so, acknowledging both the source and copyright of the owners. It is the recipient\u0027s responsibility to ensure the data is fit for the intended purpose.\tContains Natural Resources Wales information © Natural Resources Wales and Database Right. All rights Reserved. Contains Ordnance Survey Data. Ordnance Survey Licence number AC0000849444. Crown Copyright and Database Right.\tOpen Government Licence\t\t\tValid\t-\nNRW_DS125325\tMetal Mine Interventions in Wales\totherRestrictions\tno limitations\tThere are no access restrictions on this data. NRW may release, publish or disseminate it freely.\totherRestrictions\t© CNC/NRW Data may be re-used under the terms of the Open Government Licence providing it is done so, acknowledging both the source and NRW\u0027s copyright. It is the recipient\u0027s responsibility to ensure the data is fit for the intended purpose. Attribution statement: Contains Natural Resources Wales information © Natural Resources Wales and Database Right. All rights Reserved.\t\t\t\t\tUnknown\t-\nNRW_DS125315\tWoodland Surveys in Dyfed/Powys 1988 using the National Vegetation Classification (NVC) Cooke \u0026amp;Saunders - ( Paper data records)\totherRestrictions\tno limitations\tInternal use as paper data. There are no access restrictions to this data provided that any perdonal data such as landowner details are redacted. NRW may release, publish or disseminate non sensitive data freely.\totherRestrictions\ttbc but likely to be open data provided no landowner details are present\tContains Natural Resources Wales information © Natural Resources Wales and Database Right. All rights reserved.\t\t\t\tUnknown\t-\nEXT_DS100682\tEnvironment Agency (EA): Local Environment Agency