wledging both the source and NRW\u0027s copyright. It is the recipient\u0027s responsibility to ensure the data is fit for the intended purpose.\tContains Natural Resources Wales information © Natural Resources Wales and Database Right. All rights Reserved.\tOpen Government Licence\t\t\tValid\tGEMINI\nEXT_DS122123\tOceanWise: Nautical Boundaries (3rd Party Data)\totherRestrictions\tno limitations\tThis dataset is wholly owned by OceanWise. Enquirers are advised to obtain a copy from the owner/originator directly, rather than NRW. NRW may NOT publish or disseminate it in its entirety.\totherRestrictions\tNRW does NOT grant permission to third parties to re-use or disseminate this dataset.  Attribution Statement: © British Crown and OceanWise Ltd, 2013. All rights reserved. License No. EK001-20120402\t\t\t\t\tUnknown\t-\nNRW_DS114729\tPriority Marine Habitats of Wales: Honeycomb Worm (Sabellaria) Reefs (Archived 2012)\totherRestrictions\tno limitations\tThis data is comprised of a mixture of third party owned records and NRW records. NRW policies permits access to and release of this data under the same terms as its own data. There are no access restrictions on this data. NRW may release, publish or disseminate it freely.\totherRestrictions\t© CNC/NRW and various third party recorders 2011 NRW owns the copyright of the collation, but the ownership of the records themselves rests with the originator. There are no use restrictions on this data. Recipients may re-use, reproduce, disseminate this data free of charge in any format or medium, provided they do so accurately, acknowledging both the source and the copyright of NRW/third party recorders and do not use it in a misleading context. It is the recipient\u0027s responsibility to ensure the data is fit for the intended purpose, that dissemination or publishing does not result in duplication and that it is fairly interpreted. Advice on interpretation should be sought where required. To avoid re-using old data, users should periodically obtain the latest version from the original source.\t\t\t\t\tUnknown\t-\nEXT_DS115367\tAudit of Marsh Fritillary (Euphydryas aurinia) Habitat Management in Bridgend County Borough Council (CBC) area August 2002 (3rd Party Data)\totherRestrictions\tno limitations\tThis dataset is wholly owned by Bridgend CBC.  NRW may provide access to this dataset on request in some circumstances.  However, enquirers are advised to obtain a copy from the owner/originator directly, rather than NRW. NRW may NOT publish or disseminate it in its entirety.\totherRestrictions\t© Bridgend CBC.  NRW does NOT grant permission to third parties to re-use or disseminate this dataset. Those seeking such permission should approach the originator directly.\t\t\t\t\tUnknown\t-\nEXT_DS121984\tWelsh Government: Strategic Regeneration Areas (3rd Party Data)\totherRestrictions\tno limitations\tThis dataset is wholly owned by Welsh Government. NRW may provide access to this dataset on request in some circumstances.  However, enquirers are advised to obtain a copy from the owner/originator directly, rather than NRW. NRW may NOT publish or disseminate it in its entirety.\totherRestrictions\t© Crown Copyright: Welsh Government. NRW does NOT grant permission to third parties to re-use or disseminate this dataset. Those seeking such permission should approach the originator directly. Attribution Statement: © Crown copyright: Welsh Government © Crown Copyright and database right 2016. Ordnance Survey 100021874\t\t\t\t\tUnknown\t-\nEXT_DS100789\tCadw: Scheduled Ancient Monument (SAM) (3rd Party Data)\totherRestrictions\tno limitations\tThis dataset is wholly owned by Cadw. Cadw\u0027s use of data information statement: \u0027There are no use restrictions on this data. Recipients may re-use, reproduce, disseminate this data free of charge in any format or medium, provided they do so accurately, acknowledging both the source and copyright as specified, and do not use it in a misleading context. It is the recipient\u0027s responsibility to ensure the data is fit for the intended purpose, that dissemination or publishing does not result in duplication, and that it is fairly interpreted.\u0027\totherRestrictions\t© Cadw Data may be re-used under the terms of the Open Government Licence providing it is done so, acknowledging both the source and Cadw\u0027s copyright. It is the recipient\u0027s responsibility to ensure the data is fit for the intended purpose. Attribution Statement: Designated Historic Asset GIS Data, The Welsh Historic Environment Service (Cadw), 2018, licensed under the Open Government Licence http://www.nationalarchives.gov.uk/doc/open-government-licence/version/3/\t\t\t\t\tUnknown\t-\nEXT_DS112485\tBritish Geological Survey (BGS): Maps and Memoirs (3rd Party Data)\totherRestrictions\tno limitations\tThis memoirs and reports are wholly owned by The British Geological Society. NRW may provide access to this dataset on request in some circumstances.  However, enquirers are advised to obtain a copy from the owner/originator directly, rather than NRW. NRW may NOT publish or disseminate it in its entirety. There are no access restrictions to the GIS layer. NRW owns the layer and it may be released, published and disseminated freely.\totherRestrictions\t© BGS and NRW  There are no use restrictions on NRW owned data (GIS layer).  NRW data may be re-used under provision and in line with the terms of a NRW licence. NRW does NOT grant permission to disseminate or re-use any data that is not labelled as NRW ownership.  Those seeking such permission should approach the originator directly.\t\t\t\t\tUnknown\t-\nEXT_DS119306\tForestry Commission England (FCE): National Forest Estate Ownership England (3rd Party Data)\totherRestrictions\tno limitations\tThis dataset is wholly owned by The Forestry Commission. There are no access restrictions on this data. NRW may release, publish or disseminate it freely.\totherRestrictions\t© The Forestry Commission.  Da