minate it freely.\totherRestrictions\t© CNC/NRW and Coastal Surveillance Unit Data may be re-used under the terms of the Open Government Licence providing it is done so, acknowledging both the source and NRW\u0027s copyright. It is the recipient\u0027s responsibility to ensure the data is fit for the intended purpose.\tContains Natural Resources Wales information © Natural Resources Wales and Database Right. All rights Reserved.\t\t\t\tValid\tMEDIN\nNRW_DS23774\tWelsh Invertebrate Database (WID)\totherRestrictions\tno limitations\tPart of this dataset is sensitive and restricted. The sensitive data is as follows: a) Records of numbers and location (at more detailed scale than 10km) of freshwater pearl mussel b) Personal contact details (NB. Name of recorder/determiner accompanying the record are not sensitive). c) Some data has been provided on the condition that it remains confidential. d) Unvalidated records will be withheld until validation complete e) Records identified as unreliable where no further validation can be carried out will also be withheld. Sensitive data must be kept confidential; general release is not permitted due to risk of harm to the environment or third parties.  Sensitive data may only be released under an appropriate NRW Licence. Requests should be referred to NRW\u0027s Access to Information Officer. Data may be released freely if the sensitive records are removed in advance, or shown only at a coarser scale.\totherRestrictions\t© CNC/NRW 2008 Recipients may only re-use sensitive data in strict confidence under the terms of an appropriate NRW Licence or equivalent. No publication or dissemination is permitted, except if sensitive records are removed in advance, or shown only at a coarser scale. At a spatial scale at which the records are considered non-sensitive then there are no use restrictions on this data, including for commercial and research purposes. Recipients may re-use, reproduce, disseminate this data free of charge in any format or medium, provided they do so accurately, acknowledging both the source and NRW\u0027s copyright, and do not use it in a misleading context. It is the recipient\u0027s responsibility to ensure the data is fit for the intended purpose, that dissemination or publishing does not result in duplication, and that it is fairly interpreted. Advice on interpretation should be sought where required. To avoid re-using old data, users should periodically obtain the latest version from the original source.   Part of this dataset is sensitive and restricted. The sensitive data is as follows - Freshwater Pearl Mussel (Margaritifera margaritifera ).  Sensitive data must be kept confidential; general release is not permitted due to risk of harm to the environment or third parties. Sensitive data may only be released under an appropriate NRW Licence. Requests should be referred to NRW\u0027s Access to Information Officer. Data may be released freely if the sensitive records are removed in advance, or shown only at a coarser scale.\t\t\t\t\tUnknown\t-\nNRW_DS45523\tPeregrine breeding population surveillance in Pembrokeshire (1981-2013)\totherRestrictions\tno limitations\tThis data is jointly owned by NRW and Pembrokeshire Bird Group.  Part of this dataset is sensitive and restricted. The sensitive data is as follows; the exact location of peregrine nest sites.  Sensitive data must be kept confidential; general release is not permitted due to risk of harm to the environment or third parties.  Sensitive data may only be released under an appropriate NRW Licence. Data may be released freely if the sensitive records are removed in advance, or shown only at a coarser scale. [See NRW Operational Guidance Note: NRW Ecological Data exempt from general release under EIR]\totherRestrictions\t© CNC/NRW and Pembrokeshire Bird Group. 2013. Recipients may only re-use sensitive data in strict confidence under the terms of an appropriate NRW Licence.  No publication or dissemination is permitted, except if sensitive records are removed in advance, or shown only at a coarser scale.\t\t\t\t\tUnknown\t-\nEXT_DS125513\tPackaging Regulations Approved Schemes (3rd Party Data)\totherRestrictions\tno limitations\tThis dataset is wholly owned by Environment Agency EA. NRW may provide access to this dataset on request, however, enquirers are advised to request access from the owner/originator directly, rather than NRW\totherRestrictions\t© Environment Agenc. Data may be re-used under the terms of the 3rd Party Open Data licence. It is the recipient\u0027s responsibility to ensure the data is fit for the intended purpose.\t© Environment Agency copyright and/or database right 2019. All rights reserved.\tThird Party Open\t\t\tUnknown\t-\nNRW_DS24307\tDormouse Database (1905 - 2004)\totherRestrictions\tno limitations\tThere are no access restrictions to this data. NRW may release, publish or disseminate it freely.\totherRestrictions\t© CNC/NRW, 2004.   Data may be re-used under the terms of the Open Government Licence providing it is done so, acknowledging both the source and NRW\u0027s copyright. It is the recipient\u0027s responsibility to ensure the data is fit for the intended purpose. Attribution statement: Contains Natural Resources Wales information © Natural Resources Wales and Database Right. All rights Reserved.\t\t\t\t\tUnknown\t-\nNRW_DS112405\t2010 Countryside Council for Wales, Intertidal species diversity layer\totherRestrictions\tno limitations\tThere are no access restrictions to this data. NRW may release, publish or disseminate it freely.\totherRestrictions\t© CNC/NRW 2010 There are no use restrictions on this data.  There are no use restrictions on this data.  Recipients may re-use, reproduce, disseminate this data free of charge in any format or medium, provided they do so accurately, acknowledging both the source and NRW\u0027s copyright, and do not use it in a misleading context. It is the recipient\u0027s responsibility to ensure the data is fit for the intended purpose, that dissemination or publishing does not result in duplication, and that it is fairly interpreted. Advice on interpretation should be sought where required. To avoid re-using old data, users should periodically obtain the latest version from the original source.\t\t\t\t\tUnknown\t-\nEXT_DS125070\tCardiff Bay Barrage Fisheries Monitoring Programme (3rd Party Data)\totherRestrictions\tno limitations\tThis dataset is wholly owned by Cardiff Harbour Authority (The City of Cardiff Council). NRW may provide access to this dataset on request, however, enquirers are advised to request access from the owner/originator directly - cardiffharbour@cardiff.gov.uk - rather than NRW.\totherRestrictions\tData may be re-used under the terms of the Open Government Licence providing it is done so, acknowledging both the source and owners copyright. It is the recipient\u0027s responsibility to ensure the data is fit for the intended purpose.\t© The City of Cardiff Council - Cardiff Harbour Authority\tThird Party Open\t\t\tUnknown\t-\nNRW_DS24337\tWelsh Lesser Horseshoe Bat (Rhinolophus hipposideros) Summer Roost Surveillance Database (1987-2013)\totherRestrictions\tno limitations\tPart of this dataset is sensitive and restricted as it contains data exempt from general release under EIR.  Sensitive data must be kept confidential; general release is not permitted due to risk of harm to the environment or third parties. The sensitive data is as follows; 1) Location of bat roosts in private buildings or underground sites, shown at a more detailed scale than 1km square (4 figure grid reference). Disclosure would adversely affect the protection of the species due to risk of disturbance and alienation of the landowner.  2) Names and addresses of landowners, and names of recorders for which NRW does not have consent to release.\totherRestrictions\t© CNC/NRW  Data may be re-used under provision and in line with the terms of a NRW licence and NRWs guidance on Ecological data exempt from general release.\t\t\t\t\tUnknown\t-\nNRW_DS24258\tStanding Waters Database (Lakes)\totherRestrictions\tno limitations\tCCW is legally obliged to give public access to the data and information which it holds unless specific legal exceptions apply, for example, if the data is personal or if release of the data would result in environmental harm.  As the database contains cross-agency data, agreement of a representative of the Freshwater Lead Coordination Network (LCN) must be obtained and contractors must sign a data licence agreement (JNCC-recommended ), before the database can be issued.\totherRestrictions\tThe Joint Nature Conservation Committee (JNCC) owns the database design, whilst the contained data is owned by the three country agencies, Scottish Natural Heritage (SNH), CCW and English Nature (EN).   © CCGC/CCW 2004. CCW data may be used for non-commercial and internal business purposes only. It may be interrogated, imported into your own system and merged with other data, providing it is not factually altered. You may duplicate and publish short extracts of raw data and any findings and other information derived from the data, providing CCW is acknowledged. You may not copy the dataset or transfer it to others; additional copies can be obtained from CCW.\t\t\t\t\tUnknown\t-\nEXT_DS125406\tSevern Lower Seagrass Project - Seagrass Aerial Imagery Test 2022 (3rd Party Data)\totherRestrictions\tno limitations\tThis dataset is wholly owned by Project Seagrass. NRW may provide access to this dataset on request in some limited circumstances. However, enquirers are advised to request access from the owner/originator directly, rather than NRW. NRW may NOT publish or disseminate it in its entirety.\totherRestrictions\t© Project Seagrass. NRW does NOT grant permission to third parties to re-use or disseminate this dataset. Those seeking such permission should approach the originator directly.\t© Project Seagrass. All rights reserved.\tThird Party Conditional\t\t\tUnknown\t-\nNRW_DS24311\tMapinfo Habitats Database on Candidate Special Areas of Conservation (cSACs)\totherRestrictions\tno limitations\tNRW is legally obliged to give public access to the data and information which it holds unless specific legal exceptions apply, for example, if the data is personal or if release of the data would result in environmental harm.\totherRestrictions\t© CNC/NRW You may reproduce this dataset free of charge for non-commercial and internal business purposes in any format or medium, provided that you do so accurately, acknowledging both the source and NRW\u0027s copyright, and do not use it in a misleading context. To avoid using old information, we recommend that you obtain the latest version from the original source.\t\t\t\t\tUnknown\t-\nEXT_DS124768\tEnvironment Agency (EA): Area of Interest (3rd Party Data)\totherRestrictions\tno limitations\tThis dataset is wholly owned by the Environment Agency and is considered OS derived data and therefore jointly owned with Ordnance Survey. NRW may provide access to this dataset on request in some circumstances.  However, enquirers are advised to obtain a copy from the owner/originator directly, rather than NRW. NRW may NOT publish or disseminate it in its entirety.\totherRestrictions\t© Environment Agency and © Crown copyright. All rights reserved.  NRW does NOT grant permission to third parties to re-use or disseminate this dataset. Those seeking such permission should approach the originator directly. Those seeking commercial re-use may require a commercial licence available from the OS.  For internal use in NRW please use the following OS acknowledgement - © Environment Agency and © Crown copyright.  All rights reserved. Natural Resources Wales OS Licence number: AC0000849444.\t\t\t\t\tUnknown\t-\nNRW_DS161352\tAn Evaluation of the Current Use of Farmed vs Wild-caught Ragworm bait in Wales - Survey Results\totherRestrictions\tINSPIRE_Directive_Article13_1f\tPart of this dataset is sensitive, and access may be restricted under GDPR Legislation. NRW may NOT publish or disseminate the sensitive data. Requests should be referred to NRW\u0027s Access to Information Officer. However, there are no access restrictions on non-sensitive data. NRW may release, publish or disseminate a redacted version of the data freely.\totherRestrictions\t© CNC/NRW Data may be re-used under provision and in line with the terms of a NRW licence.\tContains Natural Resources Wales information © Natural Resources Wales and Database Right. All rights Reserved.\tNRW Conditional\t\t\tValid\t-\nEXT_DS124611\tEnvironment Agency (EA): Integrated Height Model data (3rd Party Data)\totherRestrictions\tno limitations\tThis dataset is wholly owned by the Environment Agency. NRW may provide access to this dataset on request in some circumstances. However, enquirers are advised to obtain a copy from the owner/originator directly, rather than NRW. NRW may NOT publish or disseminate it in its entirety.\totherRestrictions\tNRW does NOT grant permission to third parties to re-use or disseminate this dataset. Those seeking such permission should approach the originator directly. Attribution statement: Contains Environment Agency information © Environment Agency and database right. All rights reserved. Includes Natural Resources Wales LiDAR information © Natural Resources Wales and database right. All rights reserved. Includes APBG licenced DTM data © Getmapping Plc and Bluesky International Limited [2015].\t\t\t\t\tUnknown\t-\nNRW_DS109802\tMarine Intertidal Phase 1 Species\totherRestrictions\tno limitations\tPart of this dataset is also sensitive and restricted. The sensitive data is as follows; Ostrea edulis.. Sensitive data must be kept confidential; general release, is not permitted due to risk of harm to the environment or third parties.\totherRestrictions\t© CNC/NRW Data may be re-used under provision and in line with the terms of a NRW licence and NRWs guidance on Ecological data exempt from general release.\tContains Natural Resources Wales information © Natural Resources Wales and Database Right. All rights Reserved.\tNRW Conditional\t\t\tValid\tMEDIN\nEXT_DS125192\tRWE Seahorse Hippocampus guttulatus records (3rd Party Data)\totherRestrictions\tno limitations\tThis dataset is wholly owned by RWE. Part of this dataset is sensitive and restricted as it contains data exempt from general release under EIR. Sensitive data must be kept confidential; general release is not permitted due to risk of harm to the environment or third parties. See NRW guidance on Ecological data and information exempt from general release - https://naturalresources.wales/evidence-and-data/accessing-our-data/ecological-data-exempt-from-general-release/?lang\u003den However, there are no access restrictions on non-sensitive data. NRW may release, publish or disseminate a redacted version of the data freely.\totherRestrictions\t© RWE The full dataset may be re-used under provision and in line with the terms of a NRW licence and NRWs guidance on Ecological data exempt from general release. A redacted version of the data may be re-used under the terms of the Open Government Licence providing it is done so, acknowledging both the source and owners copyright. It is the recipient\u0027s responsibility to ensure the data is fit for the intended purpose.\t© RWE\tThird Party Conditional\t\t\tUnknown\t-\nNRW_DS24428\tLicencing held in the Integrated Sites Information System (ISIS) Database\totherRestrictions\tno limitations\tThis data is comprised of a mixture of third party owned records and NRW records. NRW policy permits access to and release of this data under the same terms as its own data. There are no access restrictions on this data. NRW may release, publish or disseminate it freely.\totherRestrictions\t© CNC/NRW and various third party recorders NRW owns the copyright of the collation, but the ownership of the records themselves rests with the originator. Data may be re-used under the terms of the Open Government Licence providing it is done so, acknowledging both the source and NRW\u0027s copyright. It is the recipient\u0027s responsibility to ensure the data is fit for the intended purpose. Attribution statement: Contains Natural Resources Wales information © Natural Resources Wales and Database Right. All rights Reserved.\t\t\t\t\tUnknown\t-\nNRW_DS23780\tWelsh Peatland Invertebrate Survey (WPIS)\totherRestrictions\tno limitations\tThere are no access restrictions to this data. NRW may release, publish or disseminate it freely.\totherRestrictions\t© CNC/NRW 1989 There are no use restrictions on this data.  Recipients may re-use, reproduce, disseminate this data free of charge in any format or medium, provided they do so accurately, acknowledging both the source and NRW\u0027s copyright, and do not use it in a misleading context. It is the recipient\u0027s responsibility to ensure the data is fit for the intended purpose, that dissemination or publishing does not result in duplication, and that it is fairly interpreted. Advice on interpretation should be sought where required. To avoid re-using old data, users should periodically obtain the latest version from the original source.\t\t\t\t\tUnknown\t-\nNRW_DS24283\tGreat Crested Newt (Triturus cristatus) Sites in Wales\totherRestrictions\tno limitations\tThere are no access restrictions to this data. NRW may release, publish or disseminate it freely.\totherRestrictions\t© CNC/NRW There are no use restrictions on this data.  Recipients may re-use, reproduce, disseminate this data free of charge in any format or medium, provided they do so accurately, acknowledging both the source and NRW\u0027s copyright, and do not use it in a misleading context. It is the recipient\u0027s responsibility to ensure the data is fit for the intended purpose, that dissemination or publishing does not result in duplication, and that it is fairly interpreted. Advice on interpretation should be sought where required. To avoid re-using old data, users should periodically obtain the latest version from the original source.\t\t\t\t\tUnknown\t-\nEXT_DS125135\tLocal Environmental Records Centres (LERCS) Wales: All Species Data (3rd Party Data)\totherRestrictions\tno limitations\tThis collation is wholly owned by the 4 Welsh LRCs. However there are various originators of the data and each maintain the ownership over their data. Enquirers are advised to contact the collation originators directly. Access to this data may be restricted under relevant legislation. NRW may NOT publish or disseminate the data. Requests should be referred to NRW\u0027s Access to Information Officer.\totherRestrictions\t© Cofnod, WWBIC, BIS, SEWBReC NRW does NOT grant permission to third parties to re-use or disseminate this dataset. Those seeking such permission should approach the originators directly. For NRW internal use only.\t© Cofnod, WWBIC, BIS, SEWBReC\tNot Licenced for Re-use\t\t\tUnknown\t-\nNRW_DS115555\tFishMap Môn Generalised Habitat Sensitivity Levels\totherRestrictions\tno limitations\tThe following data is considered OS derived data and is therefore jointly owned by NRW and the Ordnance Survey. NRW may release, publish or disseminate this data freely; providing recipients are made aware of use restrictions (See general use restrictions).\totherRestrictions\t© CNC/NRW and © Crown copyright 2013. All rights reserved. Natural Resources Wales, AC0000849444 Third parties seeking to re-use this data require a Licence issued by NRW. It allows re-use, reproduction and dissemination in any format or medium but only for non-commercial purposes, according to the terms and conditions of the Licence. Those seeking commercial re-use require a commercial licence available from the OS.\tContains Natural Resources Wales information © Natural Resources Wales and Database Right. All rights Reserved. Contains Ordnance Survey Data. Ordnance Survey Licence number AC0000849444 .\tOpen Government Licence\t\t\tValid\t-\nEXT_DS124590\tMet Office: Bala, Alwen, Ness Gardens climate data (historic) (3rd party data)\totherRestrictions\tno limitations\tThis dataset is wholly owned by the Met Office. Enquirers are advised to obtain a copy from the owner/originator directly, rather than NRW. NRW may NOT publish or disseminate it in its entirety.\totherRestrictions\tNRW does NOT grant permission to third parties to re-use or disseminate this dataset.\t\t\t\t\tUnknown\t-\nNRW_DS45632\tYr Wyddfa/Snowdon Terrestrial Environmental Change Network (ECN) Site\totherRestrictions\tno limitations\tThis data is jointly owned by NRW and Welsh Government. Part of this dataset is sensitive and restricted. Please refer to NRW\u0027s Sensitive Features List and Guidance for details. Sensitive data must be kept confidential; general release is not permitted due to risk of harm to the environment or third parties.  Sensitive data may only be released under an appropriate NRW Licence. Requests should be referred to NRW\u0027s Access to Information Officer. Data may be released freely if the sensitive records are removed in advance, or shown only at a coarser scale.\totherRestrictions\t© CNC/NRW and WG 2014. There are no use restrictions on this data. Recipients may re-use, reproduce, disseminate this data free of charge in any format or medium, provided they do so accurately, acknowledging both the source and the copyright of NRW/ Welsh Government and do not use it in a misleading context. It is the recipient\u0027s responsibility to ensure the data is fit for the intended purpose, that dissemination or publishing does not result in duplication and that it is fairly interpreted. Advice on interpretation should be sought where required. To avoid re-using old data, users should periodically obtain the latest version from the original source.   Recipients may only re-use sensitive data in strict confidence under the terms of an appropriate NRW Licence.  No publication or dissemination is permitted, except if sensitive records are removed in advance, or shown only at a coarser scale.\t\t\t\t\tUnknown\t-\nNRW_DS161272\tDrinking Water Protected Area\totherRestrictions\tnoLimitations\tThere are no access restrictions on this data. NRW may release, publish or disseminate it freely.\totherRestrictions\t© CNC/NRW Data may be re-used under the terms of the Open Government Licence providing it is done so, acknowledging both the source and NRW\u0027s copyright. It is the recipient\u0027s responsibility to ensure the data is fit for the intended purpose.\tContains Natural Resources Wales information © Natural Resources Wales and Database Right. All rights Reserved. Derived in part from 1:50,000 and 1:250,000 scale digital data under permission from British Geological Survey. ©NERC.\tOpen Government Licence\t\t\tValid\tGEMINI\nNRW_DS161359\tNational Peatland Action Programme (NPAP) - Water Vole and Otter Records\totherRestrictions\t\tPart of this dataset is sensitive, and access may be restricted under EIR legislation. NRW may NOT publish or disseminate the sensitive data. Requests should be referred to NRW\u0027s Access to Information Officer. However, there are no access restrictions on non-sensitive data. NRW may release, publish or disseminate a redacted version of the data freely.\totherRestrictions\t© CNC/NRW. Data may be re-used under provision and in line with the terms of a NRW licence and NRWs guidance on Ecological data exempt from general release.\tContains Natural Resources Wales information © Natural Resources Wales and Database Right. All rights Reserved.\tOpen Government Licence\t\t\tValid\tGEMINI\nNRW_DS24341\tCors Fochno Invertebrates Pitfall Trapping Survey\totherRestrictions\tno limitations\tThere are no access restrictions to this data. NRW may release, publish or disseminate it freely.\totherRestrictions\t© CNC/NRW 1996. There are no use restrictions on this data.  Recipients may re-use, reproduce, disseminate this data free of charge in any format or medium, provided they do so accurately, acknowledging both the source and NRW\u0027s copyright, and do not use it in a misleading context. It is the recipient\u0027s responsibility to ensure the data is fit for the intended purpose, that dissemination or publishing does not result in duplication, and that it is fairly interpreted. Advice on interpretation should be sought where required. To avoid re-using old data, users should periodically obtain the latest version from the original source.\t\t\t\t\tUnknown\t-\nNRW_DS24227\tWelsh Raptor and Schedule 1 Bird Database\totherRestrictions\tno limitations\tPart of this dataset is sensitive and restricted. The sensitive data is as follows a) Data showing the exact location of nest sites for specified bird species, if shown below 10km sq scale.  b) Data within the database which is owned by other organisations or individuals. No permission has been given to release or publish that data. Sensitive data must be kept confidential; general release is not permitted due to risk of harm to the environment or third parties.  Sensitive data may only be released under an appropriate NRW Licence. Requests should be referred to NRW\u0027s Access to Information Officer. Data may be released freely if the sensitive records are removed in advance, or shown only at a coarser scale.\totherRestrictions\t© CNC/NRW 2004.  Recipients may only re-use sensitive data in strict confidence under the terms of an appropriate NRW Licence.  No publication or dissemination is permitted, except if sensitive records are removed in advance, or shown only at a coarser scale.  IMPORTANT: This data contains sensitive species (bird data).  Part of this dataset is sensitive and restricted. The sensitive data is as follows a) Data showing the exact location of nest sites for specified bird species, if shown below 10km sq scale.  b) Data within the database which is owned by other organisations or individuals. No permission has been given to release or publish that data. Sensitive data must be kept confidential; general release is not permitted due to risk of harm to the environment or third parties. Sensitive data may only be released under an appropriate NRW Licence. Requests should be referred to NRW\u0027s Access to Information Officer. Data may be released freely if the sensitive records are removed in advance, or shown only at a coarser scale.\t\t\t\t\tUnknown\t-\nNRW_DS123234\tDrinking Water Protected Areas Lakes and River catchments 2021\totherRestrictions\tno limitations\t\totherRestrictions\t\t\t\t\t\tValid\t-\nNRW_DS64572\tForestry Grant Scheme Recording\totherRestrictions\tno limitations\tThere are no access restrictions on this data. NRW may release, publish or disseminate it freely.\totherRestrictions\t© CNC/NRW Data may be re-used under the terms of the Open Government Licence providing it is done so, acknowledging both the source and NRW\u0027s copyright. It is the recipient\u0027s responsibility to ensure the data is fit for the intended purpose.\t\t\t\t\tUnknown\t-\nNRW_DS46322\tGrassholm Northern Gannet (Morus bassanus) Survey (2004)\totherRestrictions\tno limitations\tAccess to this data may be restricted under relevant legislation. NRW may NOT publish or disseminate the data. Requests should be referred to NRW\u0027s Access to Information Officer.\totherRestrictions\t© CNC/NRW  All intellectual property rights (including copyrights and database rights) are owned by NRW; except photographs which are jointly owned by NRW / CEH / Chris Perrins.  NRW data is issued with non-transferable licence which permits private or educational use, internal business use, reproduction and publication, subject to conditions. The dataset may not be used for commercial purposes or financial profit or gain, or sold or transferred without special agreement from NRW.\t\t\t\t\tUnknown\t-\nNRW_DS46954\tAerial Photographs of the Intertidal Areas of Wales 1996 to 2002\totherRestrictions\tno limitations\tThis data is jointly owned by NRW and CUCAP, and CR World. There are no access restrictions to this data. NRW may release, publish or disseminate it freely.\totherRestrictions\t© CNC/NRW, CUCAP, and CR World 2002. There are no use restrictions on this data. Recipients may re-use, reproduce, disseminate this data free of charge in any format or medium, provided they do so accurately, acknowledging both the source and the copyright of NRW/CUCAP/CR World and do not use it in a misleading context. It is the recipient\u0027s responsibility to ensure the data is fit for the intended purpose, that dissemination or publishing does not result in duplication and that it is fairly interpreted. Advice on interpretation should be sought where required. To avoid re-using old data, users should periodically obtain the latest version from the original source.\t\t\t\t\tUnknown\tMEDIN\nNRW_DS125005\tVisitor count data at a selection of NRW sites\totherRestrictions\tno limitations\tThere are no access restrictions on this data. NRW may release, publish or disseminate it freely.\totherRestrictions\t© CNC/NRW. Data may be re-used under the terms of the Open Government Licence providing it is done so, acknowledging both the source and NRW\u0027s copyright. It is the recipient\u0027s responsibility to ensure the data is fit for the intended purpose.\tContains Natural Resources Wales information © Natural Resources Wales and Database Right. All rights Reserved.\tOpen Government Licence\t\t\tValid\tGEMINI\nNRW_DS24263\tInventory of Marine Intertidal Phase 1 Biotope Mapping Survey Sites 1996 - 2005\totherRestrictions\tno limitations\tThere are no access restrictions to this data. NRW may release, publish or disseminate it freely.\totherRestrictions\t© CNC/NRW 2005 There are no use restrictions on this data. Recipients may re-use, reproduce, disseminate this data free of charge in any format or medium, provided they do so accurately, acknowledging both the source and NRW\u0027s copyright, and do not use it in a misleading context. It is the recipient\u0027s responsibility to ensure the data is fit for the intended purpose, that dissemination or publishing does not result in duplication, and that it is fairly interpreted. Advice on interpretation should be sought where required. To avoid re-using old data, users should periodically obtain the latest version from the original source.\tContains Natural Resources Wales information © Natural Resources Wales and Database Right. All rights Reserved.\t\t\t\tValid\tMEDIN\nNRW_DS112408\t2010 Countryside Council for Wales, Species Diversity Layer (Neighbourhood Analysis)\totherRestrictions\tno limitations\tThere are no access restrictions to this data. NRW may release, publish or disseminate it freely.\totherRestrictions\t© CNC/NRW 2010. There are no use restrictions on this data.  Recipients may re-use, reproduce, disseminate this data free of charge in any format or medium, provided they do so accurately, acknowledging both the source and NRW\u0027s copyright, and do not use it in a misleading context. It is the recipient\u0027s responsibility to ensure the data is fit for the intended purpose, that dissemination or publishing does not result in duplication, and that it is fairly interpreted. Advice on interpretation should be sought where required. To avoid re-using old data, users should periodically obtain the latest version from the original source.\t\t\t\t\tUnknown\t-\nNRW_DS24235\tInventory of British Lakes (UKLakes)\totherRestrictions\tno limitations\tThis dataset is wholly owned by CEH and University College London.  NRW may release this dataset on request, however, enquirers are advised to obtain a copy from the owner/originator directly, rather than NRW. NRW may NOT publish or disseminate it in its entirety.\totherRestrictions\t© CEH / University College London 2004.  NRW does NOT grant permission to third parties to re-use or disseminate this dataset. Those seeking such permission should approach the originator directly.\t\t\t\t\tUnknown\t-\nNRW_DS112407\t2010 Countryside Council for Wales, Species Diversity Layer (Chao2 Analysis)\totherRestrictions\tno limitations\tThere are no access restrictions to this data. NRW may release, publish or disseminate it freely.\totherRestrictions\t© CNC/NRW 2010. There are no use restrictions on this data.  Recipients may re-use, reproduce, disseminate this data free of charge in any format or medium, provided they do so accurately, acknowledging both the source and NRW\u0027s copyright, and do not use it in a misleading context. It is the recipient\u0027s responsibility to ensure the data is fit for the intended purpose, that dissemination or publishing does not result in duplication, and that it is fairly interpreted. Advice on interpretation should be sought where required. To avoid re-using old data, users should periodically obtain the latest version from the original source.\t\t\t\t\tUnknown\t-\nNRW_DS46198\tCommon Standards Monitoring (CSM)\totherRestrictions\tno limitations\tCCW is legally obliged to give public access to the data and information which it holds unless specific legal exceptions apply, for example, if the data is personal or if release of the data would result in environmental harm.  A number of species features appear on CCW\u0027s \u0027Sensitive Features List\u0027 - refer to most recent list and accompanying guidance. CCW owns the CSM performance indicators and condition assessments, though not necessarily all supporting data used to make them. Owners of supporting data may impose additional access restrictions.\totherRestrictions\t© CCGC/CCW 2004.  CCW data may be used for non-commercial and internal business purposes only. It may be interrogated, imported into your own system and merged with other data, providing it is not factually altered. You may duplicate and publish short extracts of raw data and any findings and other information derived from the data, providing CCW is acknowledged. You may not copy the dataset or transfer it to others; additional copies can be obtained from CCW.\t\t\t\t\tUnknown\t-\nNRW_DS46929\tBiodiversity Action Plan (BAP) Marsh Fritillary (Euphydryas aurinia) in Wales\totherRestrictions\tno limitations\tThere are no access restrictions on this data. NRW may release, publish or disseminate it freely.\totherRestrictions\t© CNC/NRW Data may be re-used under the terms of the Open Government Licence providing it is done so, acknowledging both the source and NRW\u0027s copyright. It is the recipient\u0027s responsibility to ensure the data is fit for the intended purpose.\t\t\t\t\tUnknown\t-\nNRW_DS24282\tMarine and Estuarine Fish Database\totherRestrictions\tno limitations\tThere are no access restrictions to this data. NRW may release, publish or disseminate it freely.\totherRestrictions\t© CNC/NRW  Data may be re-used under the terms of the Open Government Licence providing it is done so, acknowledging both the source and NRW\u0027s copyright. It is the recipient\u0027s responsibility to ensure the data is fit for the intended purpose.\t\t\t\t\tUnknown\t-\nNRW_DS45660\tChough Breeding Population Surveillance in Pembrokeshire\totherRestrictions\tno limitations\tThis data is jointly owned by NRW and Pembrokeshire Coast National Park. Part of this dataset is sensitive and restricted. The sensitive data is as follows; Chough records. Sensitive data must be kept confidential; general release is not permitted due to risk of harm to the environment or third parties.  Sensitive data may only be released under an appropriate NRW Licence. Requests should be referred to NRW\u0027s Access to Information Officer. Data may be released freely if the sensitive records are removed in advance, or shown only at a coarser scale.\totherRestrictions\t© CNC/NRW and Pembrokeshire Coast National Park 2004. There are no use restrictions on this data. Recipients may re-use, reproduce, disseminate this data free of charge in any format or medium, provided they do so accurately, acknowledging both the source and the copyright of NRW/ Pembrokeshire Coast National Park and do not use it in a misleading context. It is the recipient\u0027s responsibility to ensure the data is fit for the intended purpose, that dissemination or publishing does not result in duplication and that it is fairly interpreted. Advice on interpretation should be sought where required. To avoid re-using old data, users should periodically obtain the latest version from the original source.  Recipients may only re-use sensitive data in strict confidence under the terms of an appropriate NRW Licence.  No publication or dissemination is permitted, except if sensitive records are removed in advance, or shown only at a coarser scale.\t\t\t\t\tUnknown\t-\nNRW_DS24270\tRare Flowering Plant and Fern Data\totherRestrictions\tno limitations\tPart of this dataset is sensitive and restricted. The sensitive data is as follows; Alpine Woodsia (Woodsia alpina)  Killarney Fern (Trichomanes speciosum) Oblong Woodsia (Woodsia ilvensis)  Rock Cinquefoil (Potentilla rupestris) Wild Cotoneaster (Cotoneaster integerrimus)  Data is restricted to 10km sq scale, as there is a risk of harm to these species is full details of locations are released. Sensitive data must be kept confidential; general release is not permitted due to risk of harm to the environment or third parties.  Sensitive data may only be released under an appropriate NRW Licence. Requests should be referred to NRW\u0027s Access to Information Officer. Data may be released freely if the sensitive records are removed in advance, or shown only at a coarser scale.\totherRestrictions\t© CNC/NRW 2002  Recipients may only re-use sensitive data in strict confidence under the terms of an appropriate NRW Licence or equivalent. No publication or dissemination is permitted, except if sensitive records are removed in advance, or shown only at a coarser scale. At a spatial scale at which the records are considered non-sensitive then there are no use restrictions on this data, including for commercial and research purposes. Recipients may re-use, reproduce, disseminate this data free of charge in any format or medium, provided they do so accurately, acknowledging both the source and NRW\u0027s copyright, and do not use it in a misleading context. It is the recipient\u0027s responsibility to ensure the data is fit for the intended purpose, that dissemination or publishing does not result in duplication, and that it is fairly interpreted. Advice on interpretation should be sought where required. To avoid re-using old data, users should periodically obtain the latest version from the original source.\t\t\t\t\tUnknown\t-\nNRW_DS47082\tStorm Petrel (Hydrobates pelagicus) Census of Skokholm and Skomer Special Protection Area (SPA)\totherRestrictions\tno limitations\tThere are no access restrictions on this data. NRW may release, publish or disseminate it freely.\totherRestrictions\t© CNC/NRW Data may be re-used under the terms of the Open Government Licence providing it is done so, acknowledging both the source and NRW\u0027s copyright. It is the recipient\u0027s responsibility to ensure the data is fit for the intended purpose.\t\t\t\t\tUnknown\t-\nNRW_DS88158\tBat Roosts Database - Montgomeryshire\totherRestrictions\tno limitations\tPart of this dataset is sensitive and restricted. The sensitive data is as follows  a) Location of bat roosts in private buildings or underground sites, at a more detailed scale than 1km square (4-figure grid reference). Disclosure would adverse affect the protection of the species due to risk of disturbance and alienation of the landowner.  b) Names and addresses of landowners, and names of recorders for which NRW does not have consent to release.   Sensitive data must be kept confidential; general release is not permitted due to risk of harm to the environment or third parties.  Sensitive data may only be released under an appropriate NRW Licence. Requests should be referred to NRW\u0027s Access to Information Officer. Data may be released freely if the sensitive records are removed in advance, or shown only at a coarser scale.\totherRestrictions\t© CNC/NRW 2003 Recipients may only re-use sensitive data in strict confidence under the terms of an appropriate NRW Licence.  No publication or dissemination is permitted, except if sensitive records are removed in advance, or shown only at a coarser scale.\t\t\t\t\tUnknown\t-\nNRW_DS24253\tAll Wales Phase 1 Terrestrial - 1kmsq Access Database\totherRestrictions\tno limitations\tThere are no access restrictions on this data. NRW may release, publish or disseminate it freely.\totherRestrictions\t© CNC/NRW Data may be re-used under the terms of the Open Government Licence providing it is done so, acknowledging both the source and NRW\u0027s copyright. It is the recipient\u0027s responsibility to ensure the data is fit for the intended purpose.\tContains Natural Resources Wales information © Natural Resources Wales and Database Right. All rights Reserved.\tOpen Government Licence\t\t\tValid\t-\nNRW_DS161317\tClocaenog Forest Red Squirrel Abundancy data 2023\totherRestrictions\t\tPart of this dataset (the targeted survey data) is sensitive and restricted as it contains data exempt from general release under EIR. Sensitive data must be kept confidential; general release is not permitted due to risk of harm to the environment or third parties. However, there are no access restrictions on the non-targeted data. NRW may release, publish or disseminate this data freely.\totherRestrictions\t© CNC/NRW. NRW does NOT grant permission to third parties to re-use or disseminate the targeted survey data. The non-targeted data may be re-used under the terms of the Open Government Licence providing it is done so, acknowledging both the source and NRW\u0027s copyright. It is the recipient\u0027s responsibility to ensure the data is fit for the intended purpose.\tContains Natural Resources Wales information © Natural Resources Wales and Database Right. All rights Reserved.\tNRW Conditional\t\t\tValid\tGEMINI\nNRW_DS24352\tUnmanaged Semi-Natural Vegetation in Welsh Uplands\totherRestrictions\tno limitations\tThis dataset is wholly owned by NRW. Enquirers are advised to obtain a copy from the owner/originator directly, rather than NRW. NRW may NOT publish or disseminate it in its entirety.  Part of this dataset is sensitive and restricted as contains data ( personal details and information on private land holdings which is not for general release ) exempt from general release under EIR.  Sensitive data must be kept confidential; general release is not permitted due to risk of harm to the environment or third parties.   Requests should be referred to NRW\u0027s Access to Information Officer.\totherRestrictions\t© CNC/NRW NRW does NOT grant permission to third parties to re-use or disseminate this dataset.\t\t\t\t\tUnknown\t-\nNRW_DS87460\tThreatened Bryophyte Database (TBDB) UK (1965 - 2005)\totherRestrictions\tno limitations\tAccess to this data may be restricted under relevant legislation. NRW may NOT publish or disseminate the data. Requests should be referred to NRW\u0027s Access to Information Officer.  The British Bryological Society currently publishes all unrestricted data on the NBN Gateway.\totherRestrictions\t© CNC/NRW NRW does NOT grant permission to third parties to re-use or disseminate this dataset. The British Bryological Society currently publishes all unrestricted data on the NBN Gateway.\t\t\t\t\tUnknown\t-\nNRW_DS98736\tAreas of Outstanding Natural Beauty (AONBs)\totherRestrictions\tno limitations\tThere are no access restrictions on this data. NRW may release, publish or disseminate it freely.\totherRestrictions\t© CNC/NRW All rights Reserved. Contains Ordnance Survey Data. Ordnance Survey Licence number AC0000849444. Crown Copyright and Database Right. Data may be re-used under the terms of the Open Government Licence providing it is done so, acknowledging both the source and copyright of the owners. It is the recipient\u0027s responsibility to ensure the data is fit for the intended purpose.\tContains Natural Resources Wales information © Natural Resources Wales and Database Right. All rights Reserved. Contains Ordnance Survey Data. Ordnance Survey Licence number AC0000849444 . Crown Copyright and Database Right.\t\t\t\tValid\tGEMINI \u0026 MEDIN\nNRW_DS64578\tSpecies Licence Return Datasets\totherRestrictions\tno limitations\tPart of this dataset is sensitive and restricted as it contains data exempt from general release under EIR.  Sensitive data must be kept confidential; general release is not permitted due to risk of harm to the environment or third parties. [See NRW guidance on Ecological data and information exempt from general release]\totherRestrictions\t© CNC/NRW For Paper Records:  NRW does NOT grant permission to third parties to re-use or disseminate this dataset.  For Species Data: Data may be re-used under provision and in line with the terms of a NRW licence and NRWs guidance on Ecological data exempt from general release.\t\t\t\t\tUnknown\t-\nNRW_DS64560\tNRW Aerial Photographs of Wales\totherRestrictions\tno limitations\tThere are no access restrictions on this data. NRW may release, publish or disseminate it freely.\totherRestrictions\t© CNC/NRW Data may be re-used under the terms of the Open Government Licence providing it is done so, acknowledging both the source and NRW\u0027s copyright. It is the recipient\u0027s responsibility to ensure the data is fit for the intended purpose.\t\t\t\t\tUnknown\t-\nNRW_DS24421\tLand Agency Data held in the Integrated Sites Information System (ISIS) Database\totherRestrictions\tno limitations\tNRW is legally obliged to give public access to the data and information which it holds unless specific legal exceptions apply, for example, if the data is personal or if release of the data would result in environmental harm. Read access to the database is granted on request by the data manager whilst write access is divided into 4 separate roles dictated by financial audit requirements.\totherRestrictions\t© CNC/NRW 2015. NRW data may be used for non-commercial and internal business purposes only. It may be interrogated, imported into your own system and merged with other data, providing it is not factually altered. You may duplicate and publish short extracts of raw data and any findings and other information derived from the data, providing NRW is acknowledged. You may not copy the dataset or transfer it to others; additional copies can be obtained from NRW.\t\t\t\t\tUnknown\t-\nNRW_DS24185\tBat Roosts Database - South Wales (BATDATA-WALES) 1982-1997\totherRestrictions\tno limitations\tPart of this dataset is sensitive and restricted. The sensitive data is as follows: [A] Location of bat roosts in private buildings or underground sites, shown as at a more detailed scale than 1km square (4 figure grid reference). Disclosure would adverse affect the protection of the species due to risk of disturbance and alienation of the landowner. [B] Names and addresses of landowners, and names of recorders for which CCW does not have consent to release. [C] Some data is owned by volunteer recorders, who may wish to impose additional access restrictions. Sensitive data must be kept confidential; general release is not permitted due to risk of harm to the environment or third parties.  Sensitive data may only be released under an appropriate NRW Licence. Requests should be referred to NRW\u0027s Access to Information Team. Data may be released freely if the sensitive records are removed in advance, or shown only at a coarser scale.\totherRestrictions\t© CNC/NRW 1997 Recipients may only re-use sensitive data in strict confidence under the terms of an appropriate NRW Licence.  No publication or dissemination is permitted, except if sensitive records are removed in advance, or shown only at a coarser scale. Part of this dataset is sensitive and restricted. The sensitive data is as follows; location of bat roosts. Sensitive data must be kept confidential; general release is not permitted due to risk of harm to the environment or third parties.  Sensitive data may only be released under an appropriate NRW Licence. Requests should be referred to NRW\u0027s Access to Information Team. Data may be released freely if the sensitive records are removed in advance, or shown only at a coarser scale.\t\t\t\t\tUnknown\t-\nNRW_DS24420\tProtected Sites Data held in the Integrated Sites Information System (ISIS) Database\totherRestrictions\tno limitations\tNRW is legally obliged to give public access to the data and information which it holds unless specific legal exceptions apply, for example, if the data is personal or if release of the data would result in environmental harm.\totherRestrictions\t© CNC/NRW 2015. NRW data may be used for non-commercial and internal business purposes only. It may be interrogated, imported into your own system and merged with other data, providing it is not factually altered. You may duplicate and publish short extracts of raw data and any findings and other information derived from the data, providing NRW is acknowledged. You may not copy the dataset or transfer it to others; additional copies can be obtained from NRW.\t\t\t\t\tUnknown\t-\nNRW_DS87108\tGround truthing towed video images from North Pen Llyn horse mussel (Modiolus modiolus) reef\totherRestrictions\tno limitations\tThere are no access restrictions on this data. NRW may release, publish or disseminate it freely.\totherRestrictions\t© CNC/NRW  Data may be re-used under the terms of the Open Government Licence providing it is done so, acknowledging both the source and NRW\u0027s copyright. It is the recipient\u0027s responsibility to ensure the data is fit for the intended purpose.\t\t\t\t\tUnknown\t-\nNRW_DS99611\tNatural Resources Wales Easements Over NRW Land\totherRestrictions\tno limitations\tThis datasets contains personal and sensitive information.  Access to this information may be restricted under relevant legislation. NRW may NOT publish or disseminate the sensitive data. In addition the data is considered OS derived data, therefore it is jointly owned by NRW and the Ordnance Survey and is subject to third party use restrictions. Requests should be referred to NRW\u0027s Access to Information Officer\totherRestrictions\t© CNC/NRW and © Crown copyright.  All rights reserved. Natural Resources Wales, AC0000849444  NRW does NOT grant permission to third parties to re-use or disseminate this dataset. Non-sensitive information may be considered for re-used under provision and in line with the terms of a NRW licence.  In addition those seeking commercial re-use of non-sensitive information require a commercial licence available from the OS.\t\t\t\t\tUnknown\t-\nNRW_DS100202\tAll Wales Phase 1 Terrestrial - SurveyArea\totherRestrictions\tno limitations\tThere are no access restrictions on this data. NRW may release, publish or disseminate it freely.\totherRestrictions\t© CNC/NRW All rights Reserved. Contains Ordnance Survey Data. Ordnance Survey Licence number AC0000849444. Crown Copyright and Database Right. Data may be re-used under the terms of the Open Government Licence providing it is done so, acknowledging both the source and copyright of the owners. It is the recipient\u0027s responsibility to ensure the data is fit for the intended purpose.\tContains Natural Resources Wales information © Natural Resources Wales and Database Right. All rights Reserved. Contains Ordnance Survey Data. Ordnance Survey Licence number AC0000849444. Crown Copyright and Database Right.\tOpen Government Licence\t\t\tValid\t-\nNRW_DS87152\tMaritime Supralittoral Lichen Survey of the Portmeirion Promontory, Morfa Harlech National Nature Reserve (NNR), Site of Special Sceintific Importance (SSSI), and Candidate Special Area of Conservation (cSAC)\totherRestrictions\tno limitations\tThere are no access restrictions to this data. NRW may release, publish or disseminate it freely.\totherRestrictions\t© CNC/NRW 2004. There are no use restrictions on this data. Recipients may re-use, reproduce, disseminate this data free of charge in any format or medium, provided they do so accurately, acknowledging both the source and NRW\u0027s copyright, and do not use it in a misleading context. It is the recipient\u0027s responsibility to ensure the data is fit for the intended purpose, that dissemination or publishing does not result in duplication, and that it is fairly interpreted. Advice on interpretation should be sought where required. To avoid re-using old data, users should periodically obtain the latest version from the original source.\t\t\t\t\tUnknown\tMEDIN\nNRW_DS99635\tAll Wales Phase 1 Terrestrial - Target Notes\totherRestrictions\tno limitations\tThere are no access restrictions on to the non-sensitive data. NRW may release, publish or disseminate it freely. The associated target notes do contain personal data which may not be released without permission. There are redacted versions of these sensitive targets note available to the public.\totherRestrictions\t© CNC/NRW All rights Reserved. Contains Ordnance Survey Data. Ordnance Survey Licence number AC0000849444. Crown Copyright and Database Right. Non sensitive data may be re-used under the terms of the Open Government Licence providing it is done so, acknowledging both the source and copyright of the owners. It is the recipient\u0027s responsibility to ensure the data is fit for the intended purpose. The associated target notes do contain personal data which may not be released without permission. There are redacted versions of these sensitive targets note available to the public.\tContains Natural Resources Wales information © Natural Resources Wales and Database Right. All rights Reserved. Contains Ordnance Survey Data. Ordnance Survey Licence number AC0000849444. Crown Copyright and Database Right.\t\t\t\tValid\t-\nNR