ce, or shown only at a coarser scale.\totherRestrictions\t© CNC/NRW 2005 Recipients may only re-use sensitive data in strict confidence under the terms of an appropriate NRW Licence.  No publication or dissemination is permitted, except if sensitive records are removed in advance, or shown only at a coarser scale.\t\t\t\t\tUnknown\t-\nNRW_DS46197\tCondition monitoring of National Nature Reserves (NNRs) in Wales\totherRestrictions\tno limitations\tThis data is comprised of a mixture of third party owned records and NRW records. NRW policies permits access to and release of this data under the same terms as its own data.  There are no access restrictions on this data. NRW may release, publish or disseminate it freely.  Part of this dataset is sensitive and restricted. The sensitive data is as follows; a number of species features appear on NRW\u0027s \u0027Sensitive features list\u0027. See CCW Sensitive Features List and Guidance for details. Sensitive data must be kept confidential; general release is not permitted due to risk of harm to the environment or third parties.  Sensitive data may only be released under an appropriate NRW Licence. Requests should be referred to NRW\u0027s Access to Information Officer. Data may be released freely if the sensitive records are removed in advance, or shown only at a coarser scale.\totherRestrictions\t© CNC/NRW 2014. NRW owns the copyright of the collation, but the ownership of the records themselves rests with the originator. There are no use restrictions on this data. Recipients may re-use, reproduce, disseminate this data free of charge in any format or medium, provided they do so accurately, acknowledging both the source and the copyright of NRW/third party recorders and do not use it in a misleading context. It is the recipient\u0027s responsibility to ensure the data is fit for the intended purpose, that dissemination or publishing does not result in duplication and that it is fairly interpreted. Advice on interpretation should be sought where required. To avoid re-using old data, users should periodically obtain the latest version from the original source.  Recipients may only re-use sensitive data in strict confidence under the terms of an appropriate NRW Licence.  No publication or dissemination is permitted, except if sensitive records are removed in advance, or shown only at a coarser scale.\t\t\t\t\tUnknown\t-\nNRW_DS99419\tAll Wales Phase 1 Terrestrial - Habitat Layer\totherRestrictions\tno limitations\tThere are no access restrictions on this data. NRW may release, publish or disseminate it freely.\totherRestrictions\t© CNC/NRW All rights Reserved. Contains Ordnance Survey Data. Ordnance Survey Licence number AC0000849444. Crown Copyright and Database Right.   Data may be re-used under the terms of the Open Government Licence providing it is done so, acknowledging both the source and copyright of the owners. It is the recipient\u0027s responsibility to ensure the data is fit for the intended purpose.\tContains Natural Resources Wales information © Natural Resources Wales and Database Right. All rights Reserved. Contains Ordnance Survey Data. Ordnance Survey Licence number AC0000849444. Crown Copyright and Database Right.\tOpen Government Licence\t\t\tValid\t-\nNRW_DS24232\tImportant Welsh Bat Roosts Database (BATSITES-WALES) 1946 - 2001\totherRestrictions\tno limitations\tPart of this dataset is sensitive and restricted. The sensitive data is as follows; 1) Location of bat roosts in private buildings or underground sites, shown at a more detailed scale than 1km square (4 figure grid reference). Disclosure would adverse affect the protection of the species due to risk of disturbance and alienation of the landowner; 2) Names and addresses of landowners, and names of recorders for which CCW does not have consent to release. Sensitive data must be kept confidential; general release is not permitted due to risk of harm to the environment or third parties.  Sensitive data may only be released under an appropriate NRW Licence. Requests should be referred to NRW\u0027s Access to Information Team. Data may be released freely if the sensitive records are removed in advance, or shown only at a coarser scale.\totherRestrictions\t© CNC/NRW 2001 Recipients may only re-use sensitive data in strict confidence under the terms of an appropriate NRW Licence.  No publication or dissemination is permitted, except if sensitive records are removed in advance, or shown only at a coarser scale.\t\t\t\t\tUnknown\t-\nNRW_DS99644\tTir Cymen Farms\totherRestrictions\tno limitations\tThis dataset is wholly owned by Welsh Government. Enquirers are advised to obtain a copy from the owner/originator directly, rather than NRW. NRW may NOT publish or disseminate it in its entirety.  Part of this dataset is sensitive and restricted as contains data exempt from general release under EIR.  Sensitive data must be kept confidential; general release is not permitted due to risk of harm to the environment or third parties. Requests should be referred to NRW\u0027s Access to Information Officer.\totherRestrictions\t© WAG NRW does NOT grant permission to third parties to re-use or disseminate this dataset.\t\t\t\t\tUnknown\t-\nNRW_DS87091\tSAC Monitoring: Monitoring Great Crested Newts at Johnstown SAC and  Deeside and Buckley SAC (2003)\totherRestrictions\tno limitations\tData-set Collation There are no access restrictions to this data. NRW may release, publish or disseminate it freely.  IPR of historical records This dataset is wholly owned by Deeside Urban Wildlife Group, Flintshire County Council, and Wrexham County Borough Council. NRW may release this dataset on request, however, enquirers are advised to obtain a copy from the owner/originator directly, rather than NRW. NRW may NOT publish or disseminate it in its entirety.   The following data is considered OS derived data and is therefore jointly owned by NRW and the Ordnance Survey. Recipients must be aware of use restrictions (See general use restrictions).  Part of this dataset is sensitive and restricted. The sensitive data is as follows Great Crested Newt records. Sensitive data must be kept confidential; general release is not permitted due to risk of harm to the environment or third parties.  Sensitive data may only be released under an appropriate NRW Licence. Requests should be referred to NRW\u0027s Access to Information Officer. Data may be released freely if the sensitive records are removed in advance, or shown only at a coarser scale.\totherRestrictions\t© CNC/NRW 2004 Data-set Collation There are no access restrictions to this data. NRW may release, publish or disseminate it freely. There are no use restrictions on this data. Recipients may re-use, reproduce, disseminate this data free of charge in any format or medium, provided they do so accurately, acknowledging both the source and NRW\u0027s copyright, and do not use it in a misleading context. It is the recipient\u0027s responsibility to ensure the data is fit for the intended purpose, that dissemination or publishing does not result in duplication, and that it is fairly interpreted. Advice on interpretation should be sought where required. To avoid re-using old data, users should periodically obtain the latest version from the original source.   IPR of historical records NRW does NOT grant permission to third parties to re-use or disseminate this dataset. Those seeking such permission should approach the originator directly.  Third parties seeking to re-use this data require a Licence issued by NRW. It allows re-use, reproduction and dissemination in any format or medium but only for non-commercial purposes, according to the terms and conditions of the Licence.  Those seeking commercial re-use require a commercial licence available from the OS.  Recipients may only re-use sensitive data in strict confidence under the terms of an appropriate NRW Licence.  No publication or dissemination is permitted, except if sensitive records are removed in advance, or shown only at a coarser scale.  Restrictions apply to the following dataset: Various - Historical Newt Surveys at Johnstown SAC and Deeside \u0026amp; Buckley SAC CCW0004800000009\t\t\t\t\tUnknown\t-\nNRW_DS46136\tSeabird Colony Surveillance along Castlemartin Coastline, South Pembrokeshire\totherRestrictions\tno limitations\tThere are no access restrictions to this data. NRW may release, publish or disseminate it freely.\totherRestrictions\t© CNC/NRW 2001. There are no use restrictions on this data. Recipients may re-use, reproduce, disseminate this data free of charge in any format or medium, provided they do so accurately, acknowledging both the source and NRW\u0027s copyright, and do not use it in a misleading context. It is the recipient\u0027s responsibility to ensure the data is fit for the intended purpose, that dissemination or publishing does not result in duplication, and that it is fairly interpreted. Advice on interpretation should be sought where required. To avoid re-using old data, users should periodically obtain the latest version from the original source.\tContains Natural Resources Wales information © Natural Resources Wales and Database Right. All rights Reserved.\tOpen Government Licence\t\t\tValid\tMEDIN\nNRW_DS64573\tCasework Data held in the Integrated Sites Information System (ISIS) Database\totherRestrictions\tno limitations\tThere are no access restrictions on this data. NRW may release, publish or disseminate it freely.\totherRestrictions\t© CNC/NRW Data may be re-used under the terms of the Open Government Licence providing it is done so, acknowledging both the source and NRW\u0027s copyright. It is the recipient\u0027s responsibility to ensure the data is fit for the intended purpose.\t\t\t\t\tUnknown\t-\nNRW_DS88070\tBat Roosts Database - North East Wales\totherRestrictions\tno limitations\tPart of this dataset is sensitive and restricted as it contains data exempt from general release unde