ne layers (SeaZone licence required) - BGS habitat layers (BGS licence required) - Modelled BGS habitat communities (BGS licence required) - Deep sea habitat layers (SeaZone licence required) Some layers may only be made available at reduced resolution e.g. sensitive features.  Please refer to individual metadata entries for each of the project tasks for more information.\totherRestrictions\t© DEFRA 2010 NRW have signed a licence with regards to the access and use of this dataset. Parts of the dataset are restricted, please see individual metadata entries for details. Derived data may be used within NRW exclusively within the scope of the aims of the DEFRA project. Derived data (as listed in the licence) may not be used for commercial gain therefore derived layers must not be made available in response to requests by external organisations that may profit from their use.\t\t\t\t\tUnknown\t-\nNRW_DS115617\tSpecial Area of Conservation (SAC) Monitoring: European Dry Heath, North Atlantic Wet Heath and Rhynchosporion Habitats in Preseli SAC (2005)\totherRestrictions\tno limitations\tThere are no access restrictions to this data. NRW may release, publish or disseminate it freely.\totherRestrictions\t© CNC/NRW 2005 There are no use restrictions on this data.  Recipients may re-use, reproduce, disseminate this data free of charge in any format or medium, provided they do so accurately, acknowledging both the source and NRW\u0027s copyright, and do not use it in a misleading context. It is the recipient\u0027s responsibility to ensure the data is fit for the intended purpose, that dissemination or publishing does not result in duplication, and that it is fairly interpreted. Advice on interpretation should be sought where required. To avoid re-using old data, users should periodically obtain the latest version from the original source.\t\t\t\t\tUnknown\t-\nNRW_DS115601\tSpecial Area of Conservation (SAC) Monitoring: \u0027European Dry Heath\u0027, \u0027Northern Atlantic We